\title{An antecedent with variables}
\taxon{Example}
\date{2026-11-24}
\author{JB00}
\import{macros}

\p{#{(\text{person}, \text{age} : [n + 2], \text{occupation} : X)} where #{n} is a constant that was perhaps declared earlier.}

\p{Variables in production rules are to be read existentially. That is, this antecedent is satisfied if some assignment of its variables is satisfied by an element of working memory.}
